---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../config';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Dragon Bot 2.0"
  description="What data Dragon Bot 2.0 stores, why, who it is shared with, and how to have it removed."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl page-x pb-8 pt-16 md:pt-20">
    <SectionHeader as="h1" title="Privacy Policy" lead="Last updated: October 2026" />
  </section>

  <section class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-3xl page-x pb-24">
    <p>
      Dragon Bot 2.0 ("the bot") is an independent, fan-made Discord bot for Clash of Clans communities. This page
      explains what information it stores and uses. It is written to match what the bot actually does.
    </p>

    <h2>What the bot stores</h2>
    <h3>When your server uses the bot</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Discord server's ID and name.</li>
      <li>The Clash of Clans clan tag your server linked with <code>/setclantag</code>.</li>
      <li>The channel IDs chosen for war, raid and news posts, and your reminder-time settings.</li>
      <li>Internal markers that stop reminders being sent twice (such as which war the bot last handled).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If the bot is removed from your server, that server's settings are deleted.</p>

    <h3>When you link your account with /link</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Discord user ID and your Discord display name at the time you linked.</li>
      <li>Your Clash of Clans player tag.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To link, you enter your in-game API token. The token is used once to check with Supercell that the account is
      yours. The bot does not store it.
    </p>

    <h3>War activity history</h3>
    <p>
      When a war or CWL round ends, the bot records a result for each member of the active lineup: their player tag,
      in-game name, stars, destruction percentage, attacks used, the opponent's clan name and the war end time. This
      powers <code>/waractivity</code>. This is public Clash of Clans data, but it is kept by the bot. The command looks
      back 10 days, and these records are automatically deleted after 14 days.
    </p>

    <h3>Supercell Store session (optional)</h3>
    <p>
      If you choose <strong>Link Store (Cookies)</strong>, you send the bot a copy of your Supercell Store login
      cookies in a private message. These work like a password for that store session. They are stored in the bot's
      database and used only to log in to the Supercell Store on your behalf when you run <code>/claim</code>. This
      feature is optional and you can ignore it completely. Only link a store session if you are comfortable with this.
    </p>
    <p>
      While you are linking, the bot reads your next direct message for up to two minutes to receive the cookie text or
      file. It does not read your other direct messages.
    </p>

    <h3>Logs</h3>
    <p>
      The bot's hosting provider keeps operational logs (for example errors and command activity), which may include
      Discord usernames or IDs. They are used to run and debug the bot.
    </p>

    <h2>How the information is used</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To send war, raid and news posts to the channels you configured.</li>
      <li>To mention you in reminders when you have linked your account.</li>
      <li>To answer commands such as <code>/playerinfo</code> and <code>/waractivity</code>.</li>
      <li>To claim Supercell Store rewards, only if you linked a store session and run <code>/claim</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The bot does not sell your data and does not show ads.</p>

    <h2>Who it is shared with</h2>
    <p>The bot sends data to these services only to do its job:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Discord</strong>, which delivers the bot's messages and commands.</li>
      <li><strong>Supercell</strong>, whose Clash of Clans API receives clan and player tags to look up game data, and whose store website is visited using your session if you use <code>/claim</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Reddit</strong>, when you use <code>/receiveposts</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Railway</strong>, the cloud host where the bot and its database run.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Support and donations</h2>
    <p>
      If a way to support the bot is offered, payment is handled entirely by a third-party platform under its own terms
      and privacy policy. This site and the bot do not receive your payment details, and a payment is not linked to your
      Discord account or unlocks anything in the bot.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Run <code>/unlink</code> to remove your linked Clash of Clans account.</li>
      <li>Server admins can turn off reminders and news with <code>/adjust_reminders</code>, or remove the bot to delete the server's settings.</li>
      <li>
        To have any of your data deleted, including a Store session or war history entries, ask in the
        <a href={LINKS.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">support server</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The bot is not directed at children under 13, and Discord itself requires users to meet its minimum age.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top will be updated.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or deletion requests:
      <a href={LINKS.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dragon Bot support server</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-slate-400">
      Dragon Bot is not affiliated with, endorsed, or sponsored by Supercell. All game content and trademarks belong to Supercell.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
